WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.334
A violent attack

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.536
on a Democratic congressman's office.

00:00:03.536 --> 00:00:04.204
Representative

00:00:04.204 --> 00:00:06.039
Gerry Connolly says a man wielding

00:00:06.039 --> 00:00:09.242
a metal baseball bat injured two staffers

00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:10.777
at his Virginia office

00:00:10.777 --> 00:00:12.879
just outside of Washington, D.C..

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:14.414
Jessica Schneider

00:00:14.414 --> 00:00:15.815
is on the scene for us right now.

00:00:15.815 --> 00:00:19.185
So what are authorities saying, Jessica?

00:00:19.352 --> 00:00:21.021
Well, right now, Wolf, they're not saying

00:00:21.021 --> 00:00:23.023
what exactly the motivation here was,

00:00:23.023 --> 00:00:25.125
but sources are telling our John Miller

00:00:25.125 --> 00:00:25.959
that this suspect

00:00:25.959 --> 00:00:27.327
was, in fact, known

00:00:27.327 --> 00:00:29.195
to Congressman Connolly's officers.

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:30.630
So all of this unfolded

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:32.132
just before 11:00 this morning

00:00:32.132 --> 00:00:33.233
at the district office

00:00:33.233 --> 00:00:34.434
here in Fairfax, Virginia.

00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:36.803
We're about 20 miles outside Washington.

00:00:37.103 --> 00:00:39.139
Police have identified the suspect

00:00:39.139 --> 00:00:42.542
as 49 year old Xuan Car Tran Pham.

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:44.911
They say that he entered this office here

00:00:44.911 --> 00:00:45.812
with a metal bat

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:47.514
and then attacked two staffers.

00:00:47.514 --> 00:00:48.782
One was a senior staffer

00:00:48.782 --> 00:00:50.283
who was struck in the head.

00:00:50.283 --> 00:00:52.118
The other was actually an intern.

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:54.154
It was her first day on the job.

00:00:54.421 --> 00:00:55.555
Now, our Capitol Hill team

00:00:55.555 --> 00:00:56.756
actually talked to Congressman

00:00:56.756 --> 00:00:58.758
Connolly on the phone earlier today.

00:00:59.025 --> 00:01:00.093
He described it

00:01:00.093 --> 00:01:02.495
as a really out of control attack.

00:01:02.495 --> 00:01:04.531
He said that this attacker went inside,

00:01:04.798 --> 00:01:06.132
smashed some of the glass

00:01:06.132 --> 00:01:07.000
in a conference room,

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.135
also broke several computers

00:01:09.135 --> 00:01:09.602
And here's

00:01:09.602 --> 00:01:11.871
the Fairfax City police sergeant.

00:01:11.905 --> 00:01:12.739
Here's what she had to say.

00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:18.445
You could absolutely

00:01:18.645 --> 00:01:20.713
tell that the people inside were scared.

00:01:20.747 --> 00:01:23.616
They were hiding.

00:01:23.616 --> 00:01:25.251
I mean, someone

00:01:25.585 --> 00:01:27.153
swinging a bat around.

00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:29.889
I would be scared as well.

00:01:34.861 --> 00:01:35.995
Capitol Police.

00:01:35.995 --> 00:01:36.763
And tonight,

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:37.263
we're actually

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:38.598
learning our team on the ground

00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:39.232
has talked

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:41.101
with the father of this suspect.

00:01:41.101 --> 00:01:42.368
He says that he suffers from

00:01:42.368 --> 00:01:43.169
schizophrenia,

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:44.637
has not taken his medication

00:01:44.637 --> 00:01:45.672
in three months.

00:01:45.672 --> 00:01:47.107
And court records reveal

00:01:47.107 --> 00:01:48.942
that this same suspect actually

00:01:48.942 --> 00:01:49.509
was charged

00:01:49.509 --> 00:01:51.211
with assaulting a police officer

00:01:51.211 --> 00:01:52.078
several years ago.

00:01:52.078 --> 00:01:52.645
The charges,

00:01:52.645 --> 00:01:54.214
though, were ultimately dropped.

00:01:54.214 --> 00:01:55.415
Now, Congressman Connolly,

00:01:55.415 --> 00:01:56.449
he was actually not

00:01:56.449 --> 00:01:57.684
at this district office.

00:01:57.684 --> 00:01:59.252
He was nearby

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:01.621
at a food pantry, ribbon cutting.

00:02:01.754 --> 00:02:03.056
But he did release a statement

00:02:03.056 --> 00:02:03.723
about this.

00:02:03.723 --> 00:02:04.357
He said this.

00:02:04.357 --> 00:02:05.592
He said the thought that someone

00:02:05.592 --> 00:02:07.227
would take advantage of my staff's

00:02:07.227 --> 00:02:08.394
accessibility to commit

00:02:08.394 --> 00:02:09.729
an act of violence

00:02:09.729 --> 00:02:12.065
is unconscionable and devastating.

00:02:12.065 --> 00:02:13.933
Now, the two people who were attacked,

00:02:13.933 --> 00:02:15.168
they were taken to the hospital,

00:02:15.168 --> 00:02:17.070
non-life-threatening injuries.

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:17.637
But, Wolf,

00:02:17.637 --> 00:02:20.039
this is really coming on the heels

00:02:20.039 --> 00:02:21.608
of of many threats

00:02:21.608 --> 00:02:23.176
to members of Congress,

00:02:23.176 --> 00:02:24.277
as well as their staff.

00:02:24.277 --> 00:02:25.512
In fact, the U.S.

00:02:25.512 --> 00:02:26.312
Capitol Police

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:26.946
chief, Tom

00:02:26.946 --> 00:02:28.348
Major, testified in a hearing

00:02:28.348 --> 00:02:29.449
just last month

00:02:29.449 --> 00:02:31.417
saying that threats have gone up

00:02:31.417 --> 00:02:34.020
400% in the past six years.

00:02:34.187 --> 00:02:35.622
What's so, so disturbing?

00:02:35.622 --> 00:02:37.790
Jessica Schneider, thank you very much.

00:02:37.891 --> 00:02:39.092
She's on the scene for us.

00:02:39.092 --> 00:02:39.726
Let's discuss

00:02:39.726 --> 00:02:41.461
what's going on with Representative

00:02:41.461 --> 00:02:43.730
Veronica Escobar, a Democrat of Texas,

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:45.765
a member of Congress.

00:02:45.765 --> 00:02:46.833
Congresswoman, thanks so much

00:02:46.833 --> 00:02:47.400
for joining us.

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:49.202
What's your reaction to this attack?

00:02:49.202 --> 00:02:50.537
And staffers in Congressman

00:02:50.537 --> 00:02:52.038
Gerry Connolly's office,

00:02:52.038 --> 00:02:53.006
it comes amid,

00:02:53.006 --> 00:02:53.540
as you heard,

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:55.775
a wave of truly unprecedented

00:02:55.775 --> 00:02:57.043
violence, threats

00:02:57.043 --> 00:02:59.646
and attacks against U.S. lawmakers.

00:02:59.646 --> 00:03:00.813
Well, Wolf,

00:03:00.813 --> 00:03:03.082
my heart goes out to the staff members.

00:03:03.116 --> 00:03:03.349
You know,

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:05.251
these are public servants

00:03:05.251 --> 00:03:07.120
who go to work every day

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:08.655
and they are there to help

00:03:08.655 --> 00:03:10.056
serve constituents.

00:03:10.056 --> 00:03:11.791
And I can't help

00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:13.459
but think of my own staff

00:03:13.459 --> 00:03:14.460
and everything

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:15.728
that they've had to go through,

00:03:15.728 --> 00:03:17.430
you know, whether it is

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:21.501
horrible harassing calls or awful

00:03:21.568 --> 00:03:25.505
hateful email to the threat of attack.

00:03:25.738 --> 00:03:28.141
And we know those of us in Congress,

00:03:28.141 --> 00:03:28.975
especially those of us

00:03:28.975 --> 00:03:30.510
who survived January 6th

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:31.978
and we were here,

00:03:31.978 --> 00:03:33.746
just how terrifying

00:03:33.746 --> 00:03:35.081
all of those attacks are,

00:03:35.081 --> 00:03:36.950
we have to be very vigilant

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:38.518
and apparently our staff

00:03:38.518 --> 00:03:40.386
also has to be very vigilant.

00:03:40.386 --> 00:03:41.955
It should not be this way.

00:03:41.955 --> 00:03:43.289
Have you increased security

00:03:43.289 --> 00:03:45.592
for your staff at your offices?

00:03:45.592 --> 00:03:46.125
Yes.

00:03:46.125 --> 00:03:47.594
Over the years,

00:03:47.594 --> 00:03:49.862
I have increased security

00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:51.965
for my staff in the district office,

00:03:53.466 --> 00:03:55.602
also around my home, frankly.

00:03:55.602 --> 00:03:57.937
But it's it is still terrifying.

00:03:57.937 --> 00:03:59.606
We have to be accessible

00:03:59.606 --> 00:04:00.673
to our constituents.

00:04:00.673 --> 00:04:02.842
We have to interact with them.

00:04:02.842 --> 00:04:04.544
And every time that we do,

00:04:04.544 --> 00:04:06.846
it comes with some risk.

00:04:06.846 --> 00:04:07.747
I want to get your thoughts.

00:04:07.747 --> 00:04:09.482
Congresswoman, I know

00:04:09.482 --> 00:04:11.551
the special counsel, John Durham's report

00:04:11.551 --> 00:04:13.353
that was released earlier today.

00:04:13.353 --> 00:04:16.556
Do you support the judiciary chairman Jim

00:04:16.556 --> 00:04:17.523
Jordan's call

00:04:17.523 --> 00:04:19.559
to have to have Durham testify

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:20.593
before Congress?

00:04:20.593 --> 00:04:21.361
I know you're a member

00:04:21.361 --> 00:04:23.062
of the Judiciary Committee.

00:04:23.062 --> 00:04:24.330
What do you think?

00:04:24.464 --> 00:04:26.199
I am a member of the House Judiciary

00:04:26.199 --> 00:04:28.568
Committee and Chairman Jordan.

00:04:28.568 --> 00:04:29.902
Unfortunately, instead of

00:04:29.902 --> 00:04:31.304
using the committee

00:04:31.304 --> 00:04:32.238
as a vehicle

00:04:32.238 --> 00:04:33.773
for getting real work

00:04:33.773 --> 00:04:35.742
done for the American people,

00:04:35.742 --> 00:04:37.810
in solving the many challenges

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:39.545
that we face in our country.

00:04:39.545 --> 00:04:42.348
He has used it as an opportunity

00:04:42.348 --> 00:04:43.850
for performance,

00:04:43.850 --> 00:04:45.551
and I have not yet

00:04:45.551 --> 00:04:48.655
read the Durham report, but I have

00:04:48.988 --> 00:04:50.823
definitely had an opportunity

00:04:50.823 --> 00:04:51.791
to look through some of it.

00:04:51.791 --> 00:04:53.626
I've heard reports about it.

00:04:53.626 --> 00:04:54.360
We've spent

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:55.495
an awful lot of money

00:04:55.495 --> 00:04:57.497
as an American government

00:04:57.497 --> 00:05:01.100
on a report that essentially proves

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:02.335
no wrongdoing.

00:05:02.335 --> 00:05:04.604
But the fact that that Chairman

00:05:04.604 --> 00:05:07.707
Jordan wants to just continue this shows

00:05:07.707 --> 00:05:09.542
their their disinterest

00:05:09.542 --> 00:05:11.611
in really the work of governing.

00:05:11.844 --> 00:05:12.745
I want to quickly turn

00:05:12.745 --> 00:05:14.647
to the issue of the southern border.

00:05:14.647 --> 00:05:16.716
You represent El Paso in Texas

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:19.352
after title 42.

00:05:19.352 --> 00:05:21.387
How concerned are you, Congresswoman,

00:05:21.387 --> 00:05:23.556
that the situation there will devolve

00:05:23.823 --> 00:05:25.024
as processing times

00:05:25.024 --> 00:05:26.092
take longer

00:05:26.092 --> 00:05:28.094
and longer and facilities fill up?

00:05:28.961 --> 00:05:30.863
Wolf, I can share with you

00:05:30.863 --> 00:05:32.732
that from the inception of Title

00:05:32.732 --> 00:05:35.868
42, I and other Democrats

00:05:36.536 --> 00:05:37.704
essentially called out

00:05:37.704 --> 00:05:39.272
the fact that Title 42

00:05:39.272 --> 00:05:41.507
was only making things worse.

00:05:41.507 --> 00:05:43.876
It created a revolving door.

00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:44.977
It made it

00:05:44.977 --> 00:05:47.280
so that migrants were attempting

00:05:47.513 --> 00:05:49.315
entry multiple times.

00:05:49.315 --> 00:05:51.584
It placed a tremendous amount of stress

00:05:51.884 --> 00:05:54.087
on communities like my own,

00:05:54.087 --> 00:05:56.122
my community of El Paso, Texas,

00:05:56.122 --> 00:05:58.324
has been the site of the

00:05:59.058 --> 00:06:01.027
highest numbers of encounters

00:06:01.027 --> 00:06:02.628
both in 20, 22.

00:06:02.628 --> 00:06:04.263
And I believe the same will hold

00:06:04.263 --> 00:06:06.299
true for 20, 23.

00:06:06.299 --> 00:06:07.500
So title 42

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:09.302
should have gone away a long time ago.

00:06:09.302 --> 00:06:11.137
The administration tried

00:06:11.137 --> 00:06:12.872
but was sued by red states

00:06:12.872 --> 00:06:14.874
like my own in Texas.

00:06:14.874 --> 00:06:17.043
And so finally, it's gone.

00:06:17.043 --> 00:06:20.146
We can now create, I think, some sort of

00:06:20.346 --> 00:06:21.647
semblance of normalcy,

00:06:21.647 --> 00:06:23.716
but we can never predict the future.

00:06:24.217 --> 00:06:25.685
We don't know what's around

00:06:25.685 --> 00:06:26.452
the next corner

00:06:26.452 --> 00:06:27.687
in terms of the challenges

00:06:27.687 --> 00:06:28.621
that we face,

00:06:28.621 --> 00:06:29.222
in terms

00:06:29.222 --> 00:06:30.623
of what will be driving

00:06:30.623 --> 00:06:32.358
vulnerable populations

00:06:32.358 --> 00:06:33.726
from their homeland.

00:06:33.726 --> 00:06:35.695
That's why it is so important,

00:06:35.695 --> 00:06:36.229
in fact,

00:06:36.229 --> 00:06:37.663
more important than ever

00:06:37.663 --> 00:06:39.866
for Congress to take this moment.

00:06:40.133 --> 00:06:43.202
And finally, in a bipartisan way, act

00:06:43.202 --> 00:06:45.338
on reforming outdated processes

00:06:45.338 --> 00:06:46.973
and outdated immigration laws.

00:06:46.973 --> 00:06:48.141
And so see if that happens.

00:06:48.141 --> 00:06:49.742
Representative Veronica Escobar,

00:06:49.742 --> 00:06:51.744
thanks so much for joining us. Thank you.

